Pick a value - or a range - along a track, with a value tooltip.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/slider)

<%= embed AppicaUI::SliderPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Slider(default_value: 50, thumb_aria_label: "Volume")
Slider(default_value: [ 25, 75 ], name: "price", thumb_aria_label: %w[ Minimum Maximum ])
```

The number of thumbs follows the value: a number renders one, an array one per entry. Each thumb holds a visually
hidden native `<input type="range">` that carries the name (`name[]` for a range), the value and the focus, so the
slider submits with forms and is announced as a slider. The `appica-ui--slider` controller adds dragging anywhere on the
track and the keyboard, and keeps the fill, thumbs and tooltips in sync.

