## API reference

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `default_value:` / `value:` | `Numeric`, `Array` | `min` | One value, or an array for a range. |
| `min:` / `max:` | `Numeric` | `0` / `100` | Bounds. |
| `step:` | `Numeric` | `1` | Granularity of dragging and the arrow keys. |
| `large_step:` | `Numeric` | `10` | Shift + arrow, Page Up / Down. |
| `min_steps_between_values:` | `Integer` | `0` | Minimum gap between range thumbs, in steps. |
| `orientation:` | `:horizontal`, `:vertical` | `:horizontal` | A vertical slider fills its container's height. |
| `tooltip:` | `:auto`, `:always`, `:never` | `:auto` | The value bubble: on hover / focus / drag, pinned, or none. |
| `thumb_aria_label:` | `String`, `Array`, `Proc` | - | Each thumb's name (an array or `->(index)` for a range). |
| `format:` | `Hash` | - | Intl.NumberFormat options for the tooltip and `aria-valuetext`. |
| `name:` | `String` | - | Form field name. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Dims it and blocks interaction. |

Events: `appica-ui--slider:change` and `appica-ui--slider:commit`, with `{ value }`.

## Accessibility

- Each thumb is a native range input (`role="slider"` with `aria-valuenow` / min / max); name it with
  `thumb_aria_label:`.
- ←/→ (or ↑/↓) move by `step`, Shift / Page Up·Down by `large_step`, Home / End jump to the bounds; ←/→ follow the
  reading direction.
- The tooltip and thumb scale honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
